# Active ignores:
# CVE-2026-12151 (undici WebSocket DoS): npm-bundled undici in Node.js base image
# at /usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici. App's own undici is
# already patched. Not exploitable in production (npm is not used at runtime).
# Fix requires Node.js base image digest update.
# Added: 2026-07-06, review by: 2026-10-06
CVE-2026-12151

# CVE-2026-93748 (http-cache-semantics information disclosure): reaches the image
# only through dev-only release tooling (semantic-release -> @semantic-release/npm
# -> npm -> make-fetch-happen -> http-cache-semantics@4.2.0) and npm's own bundled
# copy in the Node base image. Absent from the production dependency tree
# (`npm ls http-cache-semantics --omit=dev` is empty) and never imported by server
# runtime code, so it is not exploitable in production. No upstream fix exists
# (4.2.0 is the latest published version), so it cannot be remediated by upgrade
# or npm override. Revisit when upstream ships a patch or dev tooling is pruned
# from the release-equivalent image.
# Added: 2026-10-03, review by: 2027-01-03
CVE-2026-93748

